{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "multiplication table of the quaternions (row times column), not symmetric: the product does not commute:\n      |   1   i   j   k\n  ----+----------------\n    1 |   1   i   j   k\n    i |   i  -1   k  -j\n    j |   j  -k  -1   i\n    k |   k   j  -i  -1\n  i^2 = j^2 = k^2 = ijk = -1 (Hamilton); ij = k, jk = i, ki = j, and reversing a product changes its sign\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "multiplication_table", "ucas": "table quaternion", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "multiplication_table", "headline": "multiplication table of the quaternions (row times column), not symmetric: the product does not commute:", "details": ["|   1   i   j   k", "----+----------------", "1 |   1   i   j   k", "i |   i  -1   k  -j", "j |   j  -k  -1   i", "k |   k   j  -i  -1", "i^2 = j^2 = k^2 = ijk = -1 (Hamilton); ij = k, jk = i, ki = j, and reversing a product changes its sign"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "multiplication table of the quaternions (row times column), not symmetric: the product does not commute:\n      |   1   i   j   k\n  ----+----------------\n    1 |   1   i   j   k\n    i |   i  -1   k  -j\n    j |   j  -k  -1   i\n    k |   k   j  -i  -1\n  i^2 = j^2 = k^2 = ijk = -1 (Hamilton); ij = k, jk = i, ki = j, and reversing a product changes its sign\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "the octonions: dimension 8 over the reals, basis 1, e1, e2, e3, e4, e5, e6, e7\n  associative: no: (e1 e2) e4 = e7 but e1 (e2 e4) = -e7\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 2, "ok": true, "cmd": "algebra", "ucas": "algebra octonion associative", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "algebra", "associative": "no: (e1 e2) e4 = e7 but e1 (e2 e4) = -e7", "headline": "the octonions: dimension 8 over the reals, basis 1, e1, e2, e3, e4, e5, e6, e7"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "the octonions: dimension 8 over the reals, basis 1, e1, e2, e3, e4, e5, e6, e7\n  associative: no: (e1 e2) e4 = e7 but e1 (e2 e4) = -e7\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 3, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "zero divisors in the sedenions:\n  (e1 - e10)(e4 + e15) = 0, although |e1 - e10| = |e4 + e15| = sqrt(2)\n  so |ab| = |a||b| fails and the sedenions are not a division algebra (from dimension 16 on, every Cayley-Dickson algebra has them)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 3, "ok": true, "cmd": "zerodivisors", "ucas": "zerodivisors sedenion", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "zerodivisors", "headline": "zero divisors in the sedenions:", "details": ["(e1 - e10)(e4 + e15) = 0, although |e1 - e10| = |e4 + e15| = sqrt(2)", "so |ab| = |a||b| fails and the sedenions are not a division algebra (from dimension 16 on, every Cayley-Dickson algebra has them)"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "zero divisors in the sedenions:\n  (e1 - e10)(e4 + e15) = 0, although |e1 - e10| = |e4 + e15| = sqrt(2)\n  so |ab| = |a||b| fails and the sedenions are not a division algebra (from dimension 16 on, every Cayley-Dickson algebra has them)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 4, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "[a, b, c] = (ab)c - a(bc) = e7 - (-e7) = 2 e7\n  not associative: the grouping changes the product (in the octonions)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 4, "ok": true, "cmd": "associator", "ucas": "associator e1, e2, e4", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "associator", "not_associative": "the grouping changes the product (in the octonions)", "headline": "[a, b, c] = (ab)c - a(bc) = e7 - (-e7) = 2 e7"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "[a, b, c] = (ab)c - a(bc) = e7 - (-e7) = 2 e7\n  not associative: the grouping changes the product (in the octonions)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 5, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "[a, b] = ab - ba = k - (-k) = 2k\n  they do not commute\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 5, "ok": true, "cmd": "commutator", "ucas": "commutator i, j", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "commutator", "headline": "[a, b] = ab - ba = k - (-k) = 2k", "details": ["they do not commute"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "[a, b] = ab - ba = k - (-k) = 2k\n  they do not commute\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 6, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  note: q is not a unit quaternion (|q| = 2): normalised\nthe rotation matrix of 1/2 + i/2 + j/2 + k/2 (v -> q v q^-1):\n  [0, 0, 1]\n  [1, 0, 0]\n  [0, 1, 0]\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 6, "ok": true, "cmd": "rotmatrix", "ucas": "rotmatrix 1+i+j+k", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "rotmatrix", "headline": "the rotation matrix of 1/2 + i/2 + j/2 + k/2 (v -> q v q^-1):", "details": ["[0, 0, 1]", "[1, 0, 0]", "[0, 1, 0]"]}, "notes": [{"kind": "info", "text": "q is not a unit quaternion (|q| = 2): normalised"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "  note: q is not a unit quaternion (|q| = 2): normalised\nthe rotation matrix of 1/2 + i/2 + j/2 + k/2 (v -> q v q^-1):\n  [0, 0, 1]\n  [1, 0, 0]\n  [0, 1, 0]\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 7, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "slerp(1, k, 1/2) = sqrt(2)/2 + k*sqrt(2)/2\n  the arc between them on the unit sphere: a = pi/2 (a rotation by pi); slerp = (sin((1-t)a) q1 + sin(ta) q2)/sin(a)\n  check: |slerp| = 1, and q1 (q1^-1 q2)^t = sqrt(2)/2 + k*sqrt(2)/2: the same\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 7, "ok": true, "cmd": "slerp", "ucas": "slerp 1, k, 1/2", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "slerp", "the_arc_between_them_on_the_unit_sphere": "a = pi/2 (a rotation by pi); slerp = (sin((1-t)a) q1 + sin(ta) q2)/sin(a)", "headline": "slerp(1, k, 1/2) = sqrt(2)/2 + k*sqrt(2)/2"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "|slerp| = 1, and q1 (q1^-1 q2)^t = sqrt(2)/2 + k*sqrt(2)/2: the same"}], "files": [], "text": "slerp(1, k, 1/2) = sqrt(2)/2 + k*sqrt(2)/2\n  the arc between them on the unit sphere: a = pi/2 (a rotation by pi); slerp = (sin((1-t)a) q1 + sin(ta) q2)/sin(a)\n  check: |slerp| = 1, and q1 (q1^-1 q2)^t = sqrt(2)/2 + k*sqrt(2)/2: the same\n"}, "isError": false}}
